cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Aura: a connection-first mathematical canvas over a typed hypergraph"
message: "If you reference Aura or the Aura Graph Format (AGF), please cite this software metadata."
type: software
version: 2.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-25"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - mathematical interfaces
  - typed hypergraph
  - direct manipulation
  - mathematical notation
  - data format
  - handwriting recognition
  - computer algebra interop
  - educational technology
abstract: >-
  Aura represents a mathematical document as a typed hypergraph in which vertices are
  mathematical objects with typed ports and edges are port bindings. The system computes
  structure-preserving ("homeomorphic") connection candidates during direct manipulation,
  produces canvas-wide discovery proposals verified by deterministic numeric sampling, and
  serialises the document to LaTeX, MathML and JSON. Aura Graph Format (AGF, draft 0.1)
  specifies the document model so that other tools can produce and consume it. The kernel
  ships with an executable specification suite covering type propagation, serialisation
  precedence, parsing, evaluation, symbolic rewriting soundness, discovery verification and
  input robustness.
